From dfb2e7b1101a8305f41767ffc8ca83b39ff440a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:16:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Notifications, do not disturb, F-key labels, a fuller
 now-playing panel

- Notifications = true: the latest notification the helper reports
  (/run/tiny-dfr/bridge/notification: when, program, title) shows for
  NotificationSeconds over the program's part of the row, with
  NotificationIcon; never while do not disturb is on; a tap takes it away.
- Live = "Dnd" (DndIcons: on, do not disturb) and Command = "Dnd" ("dnd
  toggle" to the helper); the state comes from .../dnd.
- A Text with a line break is drawn as two smaller lines (a label over a
  key name), and FnSet in an [[Apps]] rule names an [AppSets] entry shown
  over the whole row while Fn is held in that program, instead of F1-F12.
- The now-playing panel covers only the program's part of the row, so the
  Control Strip stays usable (its volume slider above all); a second tap
  on the note closes it; with several players a key switches to the next
  ("player next"), and the panel shows the player's name. Under a slider
  the panel is hidden, not drawn over it.

The PNG preview shows a made-up notification and the F-key label rows.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
